  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>620</x>
      <y>960</y>
      <w>410</w>
      <h>200</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Started only by findany gui (open(true)), in WRITER
mode. Every command that owns the index rescans the
search folders when it opens it.
Each search folder has its own library watcher and
watcher thread, and is watched recursively, including
subfolders created later.
onChange() offers a changed path to ChangeQueue if
IndexConfig includes it. onOverflow() offers the whole
search folder when the operating system reports lost
events. A rename arrives as a delete plus a create,
and the file is extracted again.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1190</x>
      <y>140</y>
      <w>440</w>
      <h>150</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Thread-safe. offer() is called from the watcher threads and
records the latest change time for each path, so a burst of
events for one file becomes a single entry.
takeReady() is called by the indexing worker. It returns a path
only once it has been unchanged for quietPeriod (2 s in the
GUI, zero in the other commands), or null when nothing is
ready before the timeout.
A folder in the queue means "rescan this folder".</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>570</x>
      <y>1270</y>
      <w>500</w>
      <h>230</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Only started in WRITER mode. Its worker thread is the only
writer of SearchIndex. requestUpdate() only offers a path
to the queue, so it returns immediately and is safe from any
thread.
Phase 1, indexFile(), makes a file keyword-searchable. Every
new path is extracted, a renamed or copied file too. A file
that can't be read is retried up to three times, then marked
FAILED.
Phase 2, embedNextBatch(), runs when no path is waiting: it
embeds the chunks that have no embeddings yet, then the file
names that have none (each with its folder's name).
Status listeners are called on the worker thread.
state takes the values of the states in SM01.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1210</x>
      <y>590</y>
      <w>450</w>
      <h>200</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Detects the file type from the file's contents and
returns its text page by page, with its type (an
ExtractedDocument). PDF pages and PowerPoint slides are
numbered; DOCX, TXT and MD come as one unnumbered page.
Must not be able to crash or hang the application:
parsing runs isolated from the app's process, with a
time limit and a memory limit.
Throws UnsupportedFormatException for formats it can't
read, an IOException if the file is locked, and
ExtractionException if the file is corrupt or
password-protected, or parsing hit a limit or crashed.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>630</x>
      <y>1740</y>
      <w>370</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Adapts a document-parsing library that can run
in a separate process (for example, Apache Tika's
forked parser) to TextExtractor. The rest of the
system never sees the library's types.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1270</x>
      <y>920</y>
      <w>280</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Splits each page separately, so every
chunk keeps its page number.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
